{
  "id": "base-set-cosmos-holo-test-print",
  "name": "Base Set cosmos holo test print",
  "category": "test",
  "description": {
    "text": "Test prints of the unlimited Base Set holos in cosmos holofoil, the pattern on the Japanese cards, instead of the Galaxy Star foil Wizards of the Coast chose for the English release; English cards only got cosmos foil with Base Set 2 in 2000. An uncut sheet of them carries the printer's note \"OK for Color & Fit – 11-18-1999\", so CGC thinks Wizards was trying the foil out ahead of Base Set 2. Unlike the Base Set 2 reprints, they keep Base Set's numbers out of 102, its copyright line and its lack of a set symbol.\n\nThey were never sold. The cards were cut from uncut sheets after they left the printer, not at the factory, and the sheet with the printer's note went to auction at Heritage Auctions in April 2023. Every Base Set holo except Machamp, which wasn't in booster packs, exists this way, and CGC had graded 32 of them by September 2023.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "CGC Cards: Cosmos Holo Test Print Pokémon cards",
        "url": "https://www.cgccards.com/news/article/12072/"
      },
